    "proof": "Write y=u+sqrt(2)*v.  Then Tr(y^2)=2(u^2+2v^2).  Since S23 has minimum three, norms 1,2+sqrt(2),2 cannot occur at height zero.  For norms divisible by 3, u and v lie in the mod-three pairing radical.  The certified radical exclusion gives minimum at least seven, whereas the three targets have trace at most twelve.  Hence no height-zero wall survives for either coefficient.",
