    "odd_coset_count": 0,
    "proof": "Use raw coordinates scaled by sqrt(8).  A norm-six vector has raw square 48 and coordinate sum zero.  In the odd coset all coordinates are odd, so exactly three have absolute value 3.  Relative to its Golay sign word those three signs reverse, and the zero-sum equation would equate one of 24,8,0,-8,-24 with four times a sum of three signs, which is impossible.  In the even coset write the raw vector as 2z.  Then z^2=12 and z mod 2 is a Golay word, hence has weight 0,8,or 12.  Weight zero would require three signed unit entries after dividing by two and cannot have sum zero.  At weight twelve, z has twelve entries +/-1 with six of each: 2576*C(12,6)=2380224 vectors.  At weight eight, there are eight entries +/-1 and one outside entry +/-2; the zero-sum condition gives 759*16*2*C(8,3)=1360128 vectors.  The Construction-B residual sum is even in both cases.  This is the complete norm-six shell of 3740352 vectors.",
